IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-52. NOUNS of a cross-reference and of a numbered item of a schedule. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Prohibition on Money Laundering Law, 5760-2000. It records two things the First Schedule shows.
-- (1) A numbering: two orders and one Act each add an item after item (18ח), and the labels they print collide on some days.
-- (2) A citation: item (18ו) cites a section that was brought in for a limited period, and the consolidation prints that section as lapsed.
-- A citation whose two descriptions differ, or a label borne by two items on one day, is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same
-- thing are the same kind. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Law's consolidation, `ext:[infil]` lines are the
-- Infiltration Law's consolidation, `ext:[SH ...]` and `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `section 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law, in force while the 2013 temporary law brings it in`
    `section 7ג of the Infiltration Law as its consolidation prints it, with a lapse marker in place of text`
    `the place directly after item (18ה) of the First Schedule`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for most limbs here: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation's list of amending instruments.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the consolidation prints the named text as lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a numbered item`

DECLARE `How long an item is read` IS ONE OF
    `to no end that the instrument which adds it states`
    `for two years, a count this row does not make`

DECLARE `A schedule item` HAS
    `the label printed` IS A STRING
    `the item is placed after` IS A STRING
    `the item is added by` IS A STRING
    `the first day it is read` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `how long it is read` IS A `How long an item is read`
    `the first day it could be over` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the first day was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the length was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
